      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `RF_SW_DIR_PATH`/`RF_SW_FILE_NAME` (and `RF_HW_*`) keys added there are only read for the dual-option image types (`IMAGE_TYPE_SW_REG`/`IMAGE_TYPE_HW_REG`, used by chips like S3NRN4V) — see `hal_vs.cc`. The S3NRN82 runs the single-image path (`IMAGE_TYPE_RF_REG`), and `get_storage()`/`get_image_file_name()` in `hal_selectImage.cc` read only `RF_DIR_PATH`/`RF_FILE_NAME` for it, with no fallback between the key sets. Without the legacy pair the file is never looked up — matches the on-device behaviour (A/B-tested, see the linked issue). The blob location `/vendor/etc/nfc/` is unaffected and matches the keys from 469739.",
